            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پنج — panj — five."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پ is Persian's own letter, one of the four the alphabet added for sounds Arabic does not have."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart — five rivers",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پنج continues Middle Persian panj, from Indo-European pénkʷe, \"five.\" Greek pénte, Latin quīnque and English five are the same word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This one an English speaker has probably already met without knowing it. Punjab is panj + âb, \"five waters\" — the land of the five rivers. So is the fruit drink punch, named for its five ingredients. The number was in the language before the lesson was."
            }
          ]
        },
